{"base_rate":0.30517711171662126,"brier":0.3356783378746594,"bss":-0.583059511554622,"bss_hi":-0.3952061648506803,"bss_lo":-0.7806638790454697,"country":"PR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.31995912806539506,"ess":446.3892004308162,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Ponce</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Ponce rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>50%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(5%), there is still roughly a <b>11%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 734 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nPONCE 3.2 NNE, 3.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.58, ranked 109 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(108&ndash;109) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>72%</td><td class='num'><b>37%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>91%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>150</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 9 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Ponce</b> <span class=\"muted\">PR</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.58</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>108&ndash;109\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>734 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Ponce &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Ponce\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0