ot sig\" cx=\"274.86347826086956\" cy=\"287.04347826086956\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 72%&amp;#10;It rained 37% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"311.87611940298507\" cy=\"246.17910447761193\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 83 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"348.3653012048193\" cy=\"263.5903614457831\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 91%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"380.28957746478864\" cy=\"258.9577464788732\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 150 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.988\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(31%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Ponce the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.41) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-1.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>-1.148</td><td class='num'>39.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>216</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>-0.581</td><td class='num'>31.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>172</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>-0.416</td><td class='num'>30.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>166</td><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'>-0.413</td><td class='num'>22.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":18.01031,"lon":-66.62398,"n":734,"n_cities":109,"name":"Ponce","offset_days":1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.12,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.04684931506849315,"n":73,"obs":0.1095890410958904,"sig":true},{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.12,"mean":0.18338235294117647,"n":68,"obs":0.19117647058823528,"sig":false},{"hi":0.41,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.32205479452054797,"n":73,"obs":0.2191780821917808,"sig":false},{"hi":0.5619999999999999,"lo":0.41,"mean":0.473625,"n":80,"obs":0.225,"sig":true},{"hi":0.67,"lo":0.5619999999999999,"mean":0.6126086956521739,"n":69,"obs":0.2608695652173913,"sig":true},{"hi":0.78,"lo":0.67,"mean":0.7171641791044776,"n":67,"obs":0.373134328358209,"sig":true},{"hi":0.87,"lo":0.78,"mean":0.8202409638554217,"n":83,"obs":0.3253012048192771,"sig":true},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.87,"mean":0.9104225352112674,"n":71,"obs":0.3380281690140845,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9886666666666667,"n":150,"obs":0.5,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.5,"rank":109,"rank_hi":109.0,"rank_lo":108.0,"reliability":0.13881380102537616,"resolution":0.014957767992215657,"slug":"ponce","station":"PONCE 3.2 NNE","timezone":"America/Puerto_Rico"}